NAME
    theme - the colours and fonts every EmuSen window is drawn with

SYNOPSIS
    /etc/EmuSen/themes/<name>.css
    /etc/EmuSen/themes/<name>.axaml

DESCRIPTION
    A theme overrides whichever of the Luna* palette keys it cares about
    and leaves the rest alone, so a two-line theme is a legitimate theme.
    Drop a file in the directory above and pick it in Preferences; there is
    no registration step and no restart. One name is one theme: if both
    formats spell it, the .axaml is the one that loads.

    The .css form is a restricted CSS - a format, not an engine. There is
    no cascade, no specificity, no inheritance and no box model, and the
    only things it can produce are colours, numbers, font families and the
    property setters listed below. The .axaml form is an Avalonia
    ResourceDictionary and is documented in EmuSen_LunaP.md section 12.

THE PALETTE
    Written inside ':root'. Each token is a Luna* resource key in kebab
    case, and setting a colour sets both halves the palette spells (the
    Color and the brush), so nothing half-applies.

    --luna-surface           tool-window background
    --luna-input-surface     text-input background
    --luna-void              letterbox area behind a game frame
    --luna-border            card edges, panel rules, splitter dividers
    --luna-text              body and monospace text
    --luna-meter-text        meter-row labels and values
    --luna-muted             hints, group headers, disabled captions
    --luna-section-header    section headings
    --luna-accent            selection, focus and the filled half of a
                             stock control - the first token in this
                             palette for something LunaP does not draw
    --luna-on-accent         whatever is drawn ON the accent: a tick, a
                             label inside a selected row
    --luna-warning           inline caution text
    --luna-error             a failure, a refusal, an invalid field
    --luna-success           a thing that worked
    --luna-info              a thing in progress, or worth noticing
    --luna-nominal           load ramp, below 60%
    --luna-busy              load ramp, 60% and above
    --luna-hot               load ramp, 85% and above
    --luna-hud-surface       the bar and the notices over a running game
    --luna-mono-font         the monospace family list
    --luna-hint-font-size    hint text size
    --luna-header-font-size  section heading size

    The key's SUFFIX decides how its value is read: '...-size' is a number,
    '...-font' a font family, everything else a colour. A font family and a
    named colour are written identically ('monospace', 'gainsboro'), so the
    value alone could not settle it.

    Colours take any CSS spelling - #RGB, #RRGGBB, #RGBA, #RRGGBBAA,
    rgb(), rgba() with alpha 0-1, and the named colours. In the eight-digit
    form ALPHA IS LAST, the CSS order; Avalonia's own #AARRGGBB reads the
    same digits backwards, and inside a .css file CSS wins.

RULES
    Outside ':root', a block styles one kind of control. The selector is
    'element', 'element.state' or 'element part', and the element is the
    control's own name in kebab case:

    button-bar        card              console-pane      dropdown
    empty-state       error-text        field-row         filter-bar
    hint-text         luna-switch       menu-bar          meter-list
    meter-row         mono-text         path-picker-row   rgba-image-view
    section-header    side-panel        split-pane        status-bar
    tabs              tool-bar

    States: meter-row.nominal, meter-row.busy, meter-row.hot.
    Parts:  meter-row .bar; filter-bar .search, .facet;
            console-pane .output, .input, .prompt;
            empty-state .message, .detail;
            card .header, .content; split-pane .rule;
            side-panel .title, .close, .content.

    Properties: background, background-color, color, font-family,
    font-size, font-weight. A value may be a token - 'var(--luna-hot)' -
    which FOLLOWS that token rather than copying it; a rule that restates a
    colour stops tracking the palette.

WHEN IT DOES NOT LOAD
    Two tiers, on purpose. A SYNTAX error refuses the whole file and leaves
    the previous theme in force: an unbalanced brace, a declaration with no
    colon, an unterminated comment, an at-rule, a nested rule. An UNKNOWN
    selector, state, part, property or unreadable value is reported and
    skipped, and the rest of the theme still applies - so a theme written
    for a later EmuSen keeps working here.

    Either way the reason is printed the same way a config file's is, with
    the line number from your file: comments are not stripped before
    counting, so the number matches what your editor shows.

    A theme that is deleted or broken between runs falls back to built-in
    WITHOUT forgetting the choice. Fix the file, restart, and it returns.

EXAMPLES
    cat > /etc/EmuSen/themes/Nocturne.css
    :root {
      --luna-surface:        #12131A;
      --luna-section-header: #7AA2F7;
      --luna-mono-font:      "Fira Code", monospace;
    }
    meter-row.hot .bar { color: var(--luna-hot); }

    ls /etc/EmuSen/themes
